  data: {
    LLM: '1. Card distribution: Each player is dealt two cards.\n2. Betting rounds: After receiving cards, players in turn may Call (match the current bet), Raise (increase the bet), or Fold (drop out and forfeit stakes).\n3. Showdown: After the final betting round, remaining players reveal their cards; the highest-ranking combination wins the pot.',
    Player: '1. Card distribution: Each player is dealt two cards.\n2. Betting rounds: After receiving cards, players in turn may Call (match the current bet), Raise (increase the bet), or Fold (drop out and forfeit stakes).\n3. Showdown: After the final betting round, remaining players reveal their cards; the highest-ranking combination wins the pot.',
    objective: 'Form the highest-ranking two-card hand (GwangTtaeng, Ttaeng, or Geut) to beat opponents and win the pot; players may fold to minimize losses.',
    gameplay: '1. Card distribution: Each player is dealt two cards.\n2. Betting rounds: After receiving cards, players in turn may Call (match the current bet), Raise (increase the bet), or Fold (drop out and forfeit stakes).\n3. Showdown: After the final betting round, remaining players reveal their cards; the highest-ranking combination wins the pot.',
    keyRules: [
      'Hand rankings: GwangTtaeng (e.g. 3-8 Gwang) beats Ttaeng (pairs); Ttaeng beats Geut (sum of values, last digit); special hands 4-7 and 3-7 override certain combinations.',
